# What never needs to reach a build.
#
# `Dockerfile` and `Dockerfile.run` both copy explicit paths, so nothing here
# changes what any image contains -- this file only stops the daemon from being
# handed a build context it will not read. Locally that context is dominated by
# `target/`, which is larger than the rest of the repository by three orders of
# magnitude, and a build that transfers it before doing anything is one nobody
# runs twice.
#
# This does not apply to the viewer image: its build context is `ui/` rather
# than the repository root, so Docker would read `ui/.dockerignore` for it. The
# `ui/` entries below are here because a root-context build has no use for them
# either, not because they affect that image.
#
# Keep this list additive and boring. Excluding something a Dockerfile does copy
# fails the build loudly, which is the right failure, but it is still a failure
# somebody has to debug.
target/
.git/
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
fuzz/target/
